{"name":"Calc Sinter","hex":"#e7e1dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calc-sinter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Abbreviation of calcareous sinter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calc-sinter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calcareous sinter","blocks":[{"text":"Calcareous sinter is a freshwater calcium carbonate deposit, also known as calc-sinter. Deposits are characterised by low porosity and well-developed lamination, often forming crusts or sedimentary rock layers. Calcareous sinter should not be confused with siliceous sinter, which the term sinter more frequently refers to. It has been suggested that the term \"sinter\" should be restricted to siliceous spring deposits and be dropped for calcareous deposits entirely."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calcareous_sinter"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Kalksinter.JPG/120px-Kalksinter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Kalksinter.JPG/250px-Kalksinter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Kalksinter.JPG/120px-Kalksinter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKalksinter.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg/120px-Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg/250px-Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg/120px-Eifelwasserleitung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c